{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791608176,"nonce":"qzD97PjWyd3B+XRDGC9a99lxbNI=","title":"Static-hot first calls wait for the whole optimisation pipeline","message":"A function whose loop runs a constant number of times (most benchmark main chunks) is compiled before its first call (0faec08b): the worker is asked for it as soon as the module is registered, and the first call waits for the code. Whole runs show the policy pays (light Mac build, 5 interleaved runs, wall with static-hot vs ZYNTAX_DISABLE_STATIC_HOT=1): collatz 182 vs 328 ms, inlined_call 58 vs 111, free_function_call 58 vs 111, method_call 89 vs 132, mandelbrot 56 vs 75, tokenize 226 vs 297, lambda_call 16 vs 23; only binary_trees (163 vs 158) and fib (32.4 vs 31.9) are marginally better without. So the wait stays, and what it costs is start-up.\n\nTimestamped traces (ZYNTAX_TRACE_LAZY + ZYNTAX_TRACE_OPT_PHASES, light Mac build):\n- nbody, 51.7 ms to its first statement: the worker starts lua$chunk at 32.0 ms, after the module's Cranelift codegen and registration; preparing the body (scratch reach, which copies and decodes the transitive closure of the chunk's callees) 5.4 ms, the passes 8 ms (drop_insert 1.2, inline 0.8 in round 0), Cranelift 2.9 ms; the main thread is ready at about 36 ms and waits 10 to 12 ms.\n- method_call, 66.5 ms to its first statement: lua$chunk compiles in 41 ms (body 33, Cranelift 8) and the first call waits 39 ms. Rounds: round 0 10.3 ms (inline 3.5, cfg_simplify 2.1, aggregate_scalarize 0.8), round 1 4.7 ms, round 2 3.1 ms (progress: 5 folds and 5 block merges), round 3 2.8 ms with no progress at all; after the rounds 7.6 ms (drop_insert 2.75).\n\nDirections, none tried yet:\n- Start the static-hot body optimisation as soon as the module is lowered, beside the main thread's Cranelift codegen and registration (about 3 ms of nbody's wait); only the final Cranelift compile needs the installed module.\n- End the round loop when a round's progress cannot enable another round's (method_call's round 3 found nothing; round 2's merges and folds could go to the fold-only fixed point).\n- Reach only the callees the inliner can take, rather than the whole closure.\n- A quick body for the first compile with the full pipeline behind it, moving the frame across at a loop header (a gradient the light build's tier ladder lacks today).","files":null}]}